{"ref":"BDB, מָגוֹר²","hw":"מָגוֹר²","html":"† III. <big><span dir=\"rtl\">מָגוֹר</span></big>  <strong>n.m. fear, terror</strong>—abs. <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳</span> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 31:14\" href=\"/Psalms.31.14\">ψ 31:14</a> + 6 times + <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 20:3\" href=\"/Jeremiah.20.3\">Je 20:3</a> cf. infr.; pl. sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">מְגוּרַי</span> <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 2:22\" href=\"/Lamentations.2.22\">La 2:22</a>;—<em>fear, terror</em> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 31:9\" href=\"/Isaiah.31.9\">Is 31:9</a>; = cause of terror <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 20:4\" href=\"/Jeremiah.20.4\">Je 20:4</a>; elsewhere in phrase, coined by Jerem, <span dir=\"rtl\">מ׳ מִסָּבִיב</span> <em>terror on every side</em> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 6:25\" href=\"/Jeremiah.6.25\">Je 6:25</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 20:3\" href=\"/Jeremiah.20.3\">20:3</a> (where as n.pr.), v <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 20:10\" href=\"/Jeremiah.20.10\">10</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 46:5\" href=\"/Jeremiah.46.5\">46:5</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 49:29\" href=\"/Jeremiah.49.29\">49:29</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 31:14\" href=\"/Psalms.31.14\">ψ 31:14</a>; <a data-ref=\"Lamentations 2:22\" href=\"/Lamentations.2.22\">La 2:22</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">(מְגוּרַי מִסּ׳)</span>.","next":"BDB, מְגוֹרָה","prev":"BDB, גּוּר⁵"}